      subs: [
        { heading: "Hosted payment page", text: "Lowest effort, lowest compliance scope, maintained by the gateway. Costs you a brief hand-off to another domain. The default recommendation for UAE stores and the route we take unless there is a reason not to." },
        { heading: "Direct API with the gateway's hosted fields", text: "Keeps the shopper on your page while the sensitive inputs stay in the provider's frame. Middle ground on effort; your checkout page now needs the script controls that apply when a provider's form is embedded in your own page." },
        { heading: "Full direct API", text: "Your server handles the payment request end to end. Reserve this for portals and products where the redirect genuinely breaks the experience, and budget for the compliance work your provider will specify." },
        { heading: "Mobile SDK", text: `Native payment sheets and wallet buttons inside a Flutter or React Native app, which is how apps selling physical goods or outside-app services normally take card payment. Apps from ${P.app}.` },
        { heading: "Platform plugin", text: "Fast when it fits. Check it is current, that it supports refunds and webhooks, and that it does not fight the checkout customisations you already have. More on this further down." },
      ],
